{
  "dom_id": "step-q89468",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Which of the following random variables follow a geometric distribution?\n\nI. The number of free throws a basketball player attempts before making a basket\n\nII. The number of families without children among $25$ families interviewed\n\nIII. The number of people watching a movie in a movie theater",
  "worked_solution": "A geometric distribution is used to model the number of binomial experiments needed before the first success.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable I follows a geometric distribution. Making a free throw is a binomial experiment, and the number of free throws needed before making a basket can be interpreted as the number of binomial experiments needed before the first success.\n\n- Random variable II does *not* follow a geometric distribution. Asking a family whether they have children is a binomial experiment, but the number of families without children cannot be interpreted as the number of binomial experiments needed before the first success.\n\n- Random variable III does *not* follow a geometric distribution. The number of people watching a movie in a movie theater is not a binomial experiment.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
